"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00116_3fae9aa74242","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### Baseline sources","status_markers":[],"text":"- §7 — corridor cross-section, Home Median, Highway, Margin, Median Reach, service crossovers, ancestral ruin, Metropolis
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00117_644c9e73efb0","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### Baseline sources","status_markers":[],"text":"- §8 — eight biomes and Anchor Points
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00122_27422394de16","block_type":"paragraph","estimated_claims":2,"parent_heading":"### What v0.5 covers","status_markers":[],"text":"<!--@3.2.2¶1-->
Away Mode establishes TRAVEL, RISK, Nodes, Reaches, route texture, Home Reach traversal, Held Reaches, Stopovers, and the qualitative ancestral-home / Metropolis orientation. Ecological Influences establishes species-relative topology, road-edge gradients, water, drainage, seasons, sound, and human infrastructure as naturalized terrain.
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00127_26f4c7ca2982","block_type":"paragraph","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### What remains unresolved","status_markers":[],"text":"<!--@3.2.3¶1-->
The corpus does not comprehensively re-rule:
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00130_1eb21d857e4c","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### What remains unresolved","status_markers":[],"text":"- the exact cross-section: Sound Wall → Margin → Highway → Home Median → Highway → Margin → Sound Wall;
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00131_5dce67f63733","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### What remains unresolved","status_markers":[],"text":"- Sound Walls as permanent playable boundaries;
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00132_5ab377e9f734","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### What remains unresolved","status_markers":[],"text":"- the distinction between the Home Median’s generated place name and the colony’s player-selected name;
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00133_5773e8629947","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### What remains unresolved","status_markers":[],"text":"- service crossovers as Reach boundaries;
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00134_5d647c07ef86","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### What remains unresolved","status_markers":[],"text":"- the road-edge / wall-edge dual character of each Margin;
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00135_059367781c66","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### What remains unresolved","status_markers":[],"text":"- Margin renewability and permanent non-buildability;
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00136_c061eafb8a15","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### What remains unresolved","status_markers":[],"text":"- whether Reaches remain whole-biome units without internal subdivisions;
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00137_1405d73b5798","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### What remains unresolved","status_markers":[],"text":"- the exact eight-biome roster;
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00138_0a01fa76f869","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### What remains unresolved","status_markers":[],"text":"- lane count remaining independent of biome richness;
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00139_d9a7aa14ebdd","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### What remains unresolved","status_markers":[],"text":"- Anchor Points as a fixed mixed bonus layer rather than gates;
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00140_aaeeffcb2486","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### What remains unresolved","status_markers":[],"text":"- the first Home Reach’s guaranteed species suitability.
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00142_345bffa62a88","block_type":"paragraph","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### What remains unresolved","status_markers":[],"text":"<!--@3.2.3¶3-->
The Ecology specification uses “anchors” in the squirrel-topology sense, but does not clearly re-establish the v0.4.6 procedural Anchor Point system or the eight named biomes.
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00147_c9508fbe3ecb","block_type":"paragraph","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### Required ruling","status_markers":[],"text":"<!--@3.2.4¶1-->
Create one **World and Corridor canon packet** that lists every v0.4.6 geography proposition and assigns:
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00150_07005598ee08","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### Required ruling","status_markers":[],"text":"- retain unchanged;
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00151_f7ed56965d79","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### Required ruling","status_markers":[],"text":"- retain with new terminology;
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00152_025f9f81d5da","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### Required ruling","status_markers":[],"text":"- revise for v0.5;
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00153_30b8a19a102a","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### Required ruling","status_markers":[],"text":"- move to content authoring;
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00154_a326c9b33c7b","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### Required ruling","status_markers":[],"text":"- or retire.
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00156_a30d112e2de6","block_type":"paragraph","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### Required ruling","status_markers":[],"text":"<!--@3.2.4¶3-->
The eight biomes should be audited after the v0.5 economy decision, because several baseline biome identities are expressed through now-uncertain resource categories such as Rigid Scrap.
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00158_e28baf8e6ae5","block_type":"paragraph","estimated_claims":2,"parent_heading":"### Required ruling","status_markers":[],"text":"<!--@3.2.4¶4-->
**Assessment:** Architecture blocker. This determines the map ontology to which Away Mode, species topology, corridor progression, and eventual Sourcebook art all attach.
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00169_b38ad19887bc","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### Baseline sources","status_markers":[],"text":"- §9 — daily beats, traffic cycles, traffic-as-weather, Wind Draft, River’s Spume, Litter
"},{"block_id":"M050-SRC-047-SURVIVORSHIP-REVIEW-001__B00170_7af823c5f477","block_type":"list_item","estimated_claims":1,"parent_heading":"### Baseline sources","status_markers":[],"text":"- §10 — Choice-Event Cards
